//| Reset overall drawdown state                                     |
//+------------------------------------------------------------------+
void
ResetOverallDrawdownState()
  {
//--- Mark the complete overall calculation as unavailable
g_overallDrawdown.ready              =
false
;
   g_overallDrawdown.initialBalance     =
0.0
;
   g_overallDrawdown.currentEquity      =
0.0
;
   g_overallDrawdown.maximumOverallLoss =
0.0
;
   g_overallDrawdown.overallFloor       =
0.0
;
   g_overallDrawdown.currentOverallLoss =
0.0
;
   g_overallDrawdown.limitUsagePercent  =
0.0
;
   g_overallDrawdown.remainingAllowance =
0.0
;
  }
//+------------------------------------------------------------------+
//| Reset profit target state                                        |
//+------------------------------------------------------------------+
void
ResetProfitTargetState()
  {
//--- Mark the complete target calculation as unavailable
g_profitTarget.ready            =
false
;
   g_profitTarget.initialBalance   =
0.0
;
   g_profitTarget.currentBalance   =
0.0
;
   g_profitTarget.targetAmount     =
0.0
;
   g_profitTarget.targetBalance    =
0.0
;
   g_profitTarget.currentProfit    =
0.0
;
   g_profitTarget.progressPercent  =
0.0
;
   g_profitTarget.remainingProfit  =
0.0
;
  }
Each reset helper clears the calculated values and, most importantly, sets
ready
to
false
. The status field is not used to represent failure or missing data. A compliance or target status becomes meaningful only after the corresponding calculation completes successfully and sets
ready
to
true
.
This gives the Part 3 financial functions a consistent defensive pattern: reset first, validate every prerequisite, calculate only with valid denominators, classify only valid usage, and publish a ready result only at the end.
Calculating Daily Drawdown From Confirmed Equity
The daily loss rule needs a reference that remains stable for the current trading day and is measured on the same basis as the live value being monitored. For Prop Firm Guard, Part 3 uses a daily equity-reference model: the reference is the account equity captured when the trader confirms the daily baseline, and current risk is measured against live equity.
The model is:
Daily reference equity
= confirmed session starting equity

Maximum daily loss
= reference equity × daily drawdown % /
100
Daily equity
floor
= reference equity − maximum daily loss

Current daily loss
= max(
0
, reference equity − current equity)

Drawdown %
= current daily loss / reference equity ×
100
Limit usage
= current daily loss / maximum daily loss ×
100
Remaining allowance
= max(
0
, maximum daily loss − current daily loss)
This avoids the earlier balance-versus-equity mismatch. A confirmed balance and current equity are not necessarily equivalent, especially when open positions already exist. Using
startingEquity
keeps the daily reference and the live measurement on the same basis. This is the model selected for Prop Firm Guard; other firms may define the daily rule from balance, reset equity, or another reference.
Place
CalculateDailyDrawdown()
immediately after
ResetProfitTargetState()
:
//+------------------------------------------------------------------+
//| Calculate daily drawdown                                         |
//+------------------------------------------------------------------+
void
CalculateDailyDrawdown()
  {
//--- Start from an explicitly unavailable calculation state
ResetDailyDrawdownState();
//--- Require the current configured daily session
if
(!g_hasDailySession)
return
;
//--- The daily rule is valid only for an active confirmed session
if
(g_dailySession.status != SESSION_ACTIVE ||
      !g_dailySession.balanceConfirmed)
return
;
//--- Validate the equity reference captured at confirmation
double
referenceEquity = g_dailySession.startingEquity;
if
(!IsValidFinancialReference(referenceEquity))
     {
Print
(
"Prop Firm Guard: Daily drawdown cannot use an invalid reference equity."
);
return
;
     }
//--- Defend against invalid daily rule configuration
double
dailyDrawdownPercent =
      g_accountSettings.dailyDrawdownPercent;
if
(!
MathIsValidNumber
(dailyDrawdownPercent) ||
      dailyDrawdownPercent <=
0.0
||
      dailyDrawdownPercent >
100.0
)
     {
Print
(
"Prop Firm Guard: Daily drawdown percentage is invalid at runtime."
);
return
;
     }
//--- Current equity may be negative after a severe account loss
double
currentEquity = g_accountState.equity;
if
(!
MathIsValidNumber
(currentEquity))
     {
Print
(
"Prop Firm Guard: Current equity is invalid for daily drawdown calculation."
);
return
;
     }
//--- Calculate the permitted daily loss from the equity reference
double
maximumDailyLoss =
      referenceEquity *
      dailyDrawdownPercent /
100.0
;
if
(!IsValidFinancialReference(maximumDailyLoss))
     {
Print
(
"Prop Firm Guard: Calculated maximum daily loss is invalid."
);
return
;
     }
//--- Derive the selected model's fixed daily equity floor
double
dailyEquityFloor =
      referenceEquity -
      maximumDailyLoss;
if
(!
MathIsValidNumber
(dailyEquityFloor))
     {
Print
(
"Prop Firm Guard: Calculated daily equity floor is invalid."
);
return
;
     }
//--- Measure current equity loss from the confirmed equity reference
double
currentDailyLoss =
      referenceEquity -
      currentEquity;
if
(currentDailyLoss <
0.0
)
      currentDailyLoss =
0.0
;
if
(!
MathIsValidNumber
(currentDailyLoss))
     {
Print
(
"Prop Firm Guard: Calculated daily loss is invalid."
);
return
;
     }
//--- Express the loss relative to the session equity reference
double
drawdownPercent =
      currentDailyLoss /
      referenceEquity *
100.0
;
//--- Express the loss as consumption of the permitted daily allowance
double
limitUsagePercent =
      currentDailyLoss /
      maximumDailyLoss *
100.0
;
if
(!
MathIsValidNumber
(drawdownPercent) ||
      !
MathIsValidNumber
(limitUsagePercent))
     {
Print
(
"Prop Firm Guard: Calculated daily drawdown percentages are invalid."
);
return
;
     }
//--- Preserve zero usage when equity remains above the reference
if
(drawdownPercent <
0.0
)
      drawdownPercent =
0.0
;
if
(limitUsagePercent <
0.0
)
      limitUsagePercent =
0.0
;
//--- Calculate money still available before the daily floor is reached
double
remainingAllowance =
      maximumDailyLoss -
      currentDailyLoss;
if
(remainingAllowance <
0.0
)
      remainingAllowance =
0.0
;
if
(!
MathIsValidNumber
(remainingAllowance))
     {
Print
(
"Prop Firm Guard: Calculated daily remaining allowance is invalid."
);
return
;
     }
//--- Classify only after all required financial values are valid
ENUM_COMPLIANCE_STATUS status;
if
(!ClassifyLossUsage(limitUsagePercent,
                         status))
return
;
//--- Publish the complete calculated state only after validation succeeds
g_dailyDrawdown.referenceEquity    = referenceEquity;
   g_dailyDrawdown.currentEquity      = currentEquity;
   g_dailyDrawdown.maximumDailyLoss   = maximumDailyLoss;
   g_dailyDrawdown.dailyEquityFloor   = dailyEquityFloor;
   g_dailyDrawdown.currentDailyLoss   = currentDailyLoss;
   g_dailyDrawdown.drawdownPercent    = drawdownPercent;
   g_dailyDrawdown.limitUsagePercent  = limitUsagePercent;
   g_dailyDrawdown.remainingAllowance = remainingAllowance;
   g_dailyDrawdown.status             = status;
   g_dailyDrawdown.ready              =
true
;
  }
The function begins by resetting the runtime state, so any early return leaves the daily calculation unavailable. It then requires a loaded session, an active lifecycle state, confirmed baseline data, and a valid positive
startingEquity
. The configured daily percentage, current equity, and resulting maximum permitted loss are also validated before any classification takes place.
The derived values are calculated in local variables first. This prevents partially updated global state if one of the later checks fails. Only after the usage percentage has been classified successfully are the calculated values copied into
g_dailyDrawdown
, with
ready
set to
true
last.
For example, with a confirmed reference equity of 20,000 and a daily limit of 5%, the maximum daily loss is 1,000 and the daily equity floor is 19,000. If current equity falls to 19,300, the current daily loss is 700, limit usage is 70%, and the result enters the warning range when the default warning threshold is 70%.
Calculating Static Overall Drawdown
Overall drawdown uses a different reference from the daily rule. Instead of resetting with the current trading day, it remains anchored to the initial challenge balance stored in
g_accountSettings.initialBalance
. The selected model is:
Initial reference
= initial challenge balance

Maximum overall loss
= initial balance × overall drawdown % /
100
Static overall equity
floor
= initial balance − maximum overall loss

Current overall loss
= max(
0
, initial balance − current equity)

Limit usage
= current overall loss / maximum overall loss ×
100
Remaining allowance
= max(
0
, maximum overall loss − current overall loss)
For example, with an initial challenge balance of 20,000 and an overall drawdown limit of 10%, the maximum permitted overall loss is 2,000. The resulting static equity floor is therefore 18,000. Add
CalculateOverallDrawdown()
immediately after
CalculateDailyDrawdown()
:
//+------------------------------------------------------------------+
//| Calculate overall drawdown                                       |
//+------------------------------------------------------------------+
void
CalculateOverallDrawdown()
  {
//--- Start from an explicitly unavailable calculation state
ResetOverallDrawdownState();
//--- Validate the fixed initial account reference
double
initialBalance = g_accountSettings.initialBalance;
if
(!IsValidFinancialReference(initialBalance))
     {
Print
(
"Prop Firm Guard: Overall drawdown cannot use an invalid initial balance."
);
return
;
     }
//--- Defend against invalid overall rule configuration
double
overallDrawdownPercent =
      g_accountSettings.overallDrawdownPercent;
if
(!
MathIsValidNumber
(overallDrawdownPercent) ||
      overallDrawdownPercent <=
0.0
||
      overallDrawdownPercent >
100.0
)
     {
Print
(
"Prop Firm Guard: Overall drawdown percentage is invalid at runtime."
);
return
;
     }
//--- Current equity may become negative after a severe account loss
double
currentEquity = g_accountState.equity;
if
(!
MathIsValidNumber
(currentEquity))
     {
Print
(
"Prop Firm Guard: Current equity is invalid for overall drawdown calculation."
);
return
;
     }
//--- Calculate the maximum permitted static overall loss
double
maximumOverallLoss =
      initialBalance *
      overallDrawdownPercent /
100.0
;
if
(!IsValidFinancialReference(maximumOverallLoss))
     {
Print
(
"Prop Firm Guard: Calculated maximum overall loss is invalid."
);
return
;
     }
//--- Derive the static minimum equity permitted by this rule model
double
overallFloor =
      initialBalance -
      maximumOverallLoss;
if
(!
MathIsValidNumber
(overallFloor))
     {
Print
(
"Prop Firm Guard: Calculated overall equity floor is invalid."
);
return
;
     }
//--- Measure current equity loss from the fixed initial balance
double
currentOverallLoss =
      initialBalance -
      currentEquity;
if
(currentOverallLoss <
0.0
)
      currentOverallLoss =
0.0
;
if
(!
MathIsValidNumber
(currentOverallLoss))
     {
Print
(
"Prop Firm Guard: Calculated overall loss is invalid."
);
return
;
     }
//--- Express current loss as consumption of the overall allowance
double
limitUsagePercent =
      currentOverallLoss /
      maximumOverallLoss *
100.0
;
if
(!
MathIsValidNumber
(limitUsagePercent))
     {
Print
(
"Prop Firm Guard: Calculated overall limit usage is invalid."
);
return
;
     }
if
(limitUsagePercent <
0.0
)
      limitUsagePercent =
0.0
;
//--- Calculate money still available before the static floor is reached
double
remainingAllowance =
      maximumOverallLoss -
      currentOverallLoss;
if
(remainingAllowance <
0.0
)
      remainingAllowance =
0.0
;
if
(!
MathIsValidNumber
(remainingAllowance))
     {
Print
(
"Prop Firm Guard: Calculated overall remaining allowance is invalid."
);
return
;
     }
//--- Classify only after all required financial values are valid
ENUM_COMPLIANCE_STATUS status;
if
(!ClassifyLossUsage(limitUsagePercent,
                         status))
return
;
//--- Publish the complete calculated state only after validation succeeds
g_overallDrawdown.initialBalance     = initialBalance;
   g_overallDrawdown.currentEquity      = currentEquity;
   g_overallDrawdown.maximumOverallLoss = maximumOverallLoss;
   g_overallDrawdown.overallFloor       = overallFloor;
   g_overallDrawdown.currentOverallLoss = currentOverallLoss;
   g_overallDrawdown.limitUsagePercent  = limitUsagePercent;
   g_overallDrawdown.remainingAllowance = remainingAllowance;
   g_overallDrawdown.status             = status;
   g_overallDrawdown.ready              =
true
;
  }
The function follows the same defensive pattern used by the daily calculation. It resets the runtime state first, validates the fixed reference and percentage, calculates the permitted loss and equity floor, then classifies usage only after every required value is valid.
ready
is set to
true
only after the complete state has been published.
The important difference is the reference itself. Daily drawdown can change when a new trading day begins and a new session equity is confirmed. Overall drawdown does not. Under this model, the initial challenge balance remains fixed, so the equity floor also remains fixed even if the account later grows.
This article implements a static overall equity floor. It does not implement trailing drawdown, end-of-day trailing drawdown, balance high-watermark, or equity high-watermark rules. Those models require different reference-update logic and should not be treated as equivalent to the implementation used here.
Tracking the Realized-Balance Profit Target
The profit target answers a different question from the two drawdown rules. Instead of measuring how much loss allowance has been consumed, it measures how much realized account growth has been achieved relative to the initial challenge balance. For Prop Firm Guard, Part 3 uses a
realized-balance target model
. The relationships are:
Target amount
= initial balance × profit target % /
100
Target balance
= initial balance + target amount

Current realized profit
= max(
0
, current balance − initial balance)

Progress
= current realized profit / target amount ×
100
Remaining profit
= max(
0
, target amount − current realized profit)
For example, an initial challenge balance of 20,000 with an 8% profit target requires 1,600 in realized profit. The target balance is therefore 21,600. Add
CalculateProfitTarget()
immediately after
CalculateOverallDrawdown()
:
//+------------------------------------------------------------------+
//| Calculate profit target                                          |
//+------------------------------------------------------------------+
void
CalculateProfitTarget()
  {
//--- Start from an explicitly unavailable calculation state
ResetProfitTargetState();
//--- Validate the fixed initial account reference
double
initialBalance = g_accountSettings.initialBalance;
if
(!IsValidFinancialReference(initialBalance))
     {
Print
(
"Prop Firm Guard: Profit target cannot use an invalid initial balance."
);
return
;
     }
//--- Defend against invalid profit target configuration
double
profitTargetPercent =
      g_accountSettings.profitTargetPercent;
if
(!
MathIsValidNumber
(profitTargetPercent) ||
      profitTargetPercent <=
0.0
||
      profitTargetPercent >
100.0
)
     {
Print
(
"Prop Firm Guard: Profit target percentage is invalid at runtime."
);
return
;
     }
//--- Read the current realized account balance
double
currentBalance = g_accountState.balance;
if
(!
MathIsValidNumber
(currentBalance))
     {
