GetOverallGuardStatus()
is the point where the three independent financial engines become one account-level view. It does not recalculate the underlying values. Instead, it reads the latest runtime states and resolves them according to a fixed priority.
The first decision is readiness. This must be checked before any individual status is consumed because a status field is meaningful only when its corresponding calculation has completed successfully. If even one required engine is unavailable, the combined result becomes GUARD_NOT_READY.
For example:
Daily     = NOT READY
Overall   = SAFE
Target    = REACHED

Guard     = NOT READY
Without the readiness check, the account could incorrectly appear to have completed the target even though the daily loss rule has not been evaluated.
Once all three engines are ready, risk takes priority over achievement. A breach is more important than a critical state, a critical state is more important than a warning, and every active drawdown condition takes priority over TARGET_REACHED.
The complete order is therefore:
GUARD_NOT_READY
GUARD_BREACHED
GUARD_CRITICAL
GUARD_WARNING
GUARD_TARGET_REACHED
GUARD_SAFE
Consider another case:
Daily     = CRITICAL
Overall   = SAFE
Target    = REACHED
