Integrating Financial Calculations Into the Runtime Lifecycle
The three financial engines are now complete, but they still need to be placed correctly inside the EA lifecycle. Their calculations depend on live account values, persisted settings, and the current daily session, so execution order matters just as much as the formulas themselves.
Part 3 integrates the financial layer at three points: immediately after a daily baseline is confirmed, during EA initialization, and during each timer-driven refresh. Together, these points ensure that the runtime states are reconstructed when the EA starts, refreshed immediately after confirmation, and then updated periodically as account values change.
